---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import appIcon from "../../../../desktop/src/renderer/assets/app-icon.png";
import { links } from "../../links";
import "./transformation.css";
---

<transformation-hero data-view="lecture" aria-labelledby="intro">
  <section class="transformation-stage">
    <div class="transformation-copy">
      <h1 id="intro" aria-label="From 看不懂 to Now I understand. EdU, your personal AI tutor.">
        <span class="hero-headline hero-before" lang="zh-Hans" aria-hidden="true">看不懂<span class="hero-question">。</span></span>
        <span class="hero-headline hero-after" aria-hidden="true">Now I<br />understand.</span>
      </h1>
      <div class="hero-description">
        <p class="hero-before">All the information.<br />None of the understanding.</p>
        <p class="hero-after">Your slides, made simple.<br />Your own AI tutor, until it clicks.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="action action-primary" href={links.download || "#download"} download={!!links.download}>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v12m-5-5 5 5 5-5M5 16v4a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h12a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-4" /></svg>
          Download EdU
        </a>
        <p>Less staring. More understanding.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="transformation-example">
      <div class="transformation-art">
        <div class="lecture-cluster" data-lecture aria-hidden="false">
          <article class="lecture-paper">
            <div class="lecture-meta"><span>Linear algebra</span><span>Lecture 08 / 42</span></div>
            <h2>2.4 Linear transformation<br />with respect to a B-basis</h2>
            <div class="lecture-columns">
              <div>
                <div class="lecture-commutative math">
                  <span>x</span><span class="commutative-arrow"><small>A = PDP<sup>−1</sup></small>⟶</span><span>y</span>
                  <span class="vertical-arrow">P<sup>−1</sup> ↓ ↑ P</span><span></span><span class="vertical-arrow">P<sup>−1</sup> ↓ ↑ P</span>
                  <span>[x]<sub>B</sub></span><span class="commutative-arrow"><small>[T]<sub>B</sub> = D</small>⟶</span><span>[y]<sub>B</sub></span>
                </div>
                <div class="lecture-highlight math">x = P[x]<sub>B</sub><br />P<sup>−1</sup>x = [x]<sub>B</sub></div>
                <p class="lecture-subtitle">Let’s start from y:</p>
                <div class="lecture-proof math">y = P[y]<sub>B</sub><br />= PD[x]<sub>B</sub><br />= PDP<sup>−1</sup>x</div>
                <div class="lecture-therefore"><span>Therefore</span><p class="math">P<sup>−1</sup>AP = D</p></div>
              </div>
              <div class="lecture-theorem">
                <p class="theorem-number">Theorem 8</p>
                <h3>Diagonal matrix representation</h3>
                <p>Suppose A = PDP<sup>−1</sup>, where D is a diagonal n × n matrix. If B is the basis for ℝ<sup>n</sup> formed from the columns of P, then D is the B-matrix for the transformation x ↦ Ax.</p>
                <h3>Proof</h3>
                <p>Denote the columns of P by b₁, …, bₙ, so that B = {b₁, …, bₙ}. In this case P is the change-of-coordinates matrix.</p>
                <div class="theorem-equations math">[T]<sub>B</sub> = [[T(b₁)]<sub>B</sub> ⋯ [T(bₙ)]<sub>B</sub>]<br />= [P<sup>−1</sup>Ab₁ ⋯ P<sup>−1</sup>Abₙ]<br />= P<sup>−1</sup>A[b₁ ⋯ bₙ]<br />= P<sup>−1</sup>AP = D ∎</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <footer>Change of coordinates &amp; similarity <span>291</span></footer>
          </article>
          <div class="lecture-scrap scrap-blue math" aria-hidden="true">[y]<sub>B</sub> = [T]<sub>B</sub>[x]<sub>B</sub><span>…but why?</span></div>
          <div class="lecture-scrap scrap-yellow math" aria-hidden="true">A = PDP<sup>−1</sup><svg viewBox="0 0 200 35" fill="none"><path d="M5 14C52-4 161-3 193 11S99 39 14 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" /></svg></div>
        </div>

        <article class="understanding-paper" data-explanation aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="understanding-toolbar">
            <Image src={appIcon} width={27} height={27} alt="" format="webp" />
            <span>EdU</span><span class="understanding-divider">/</span><span>Linear algebra</span>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 4h16v16H4zM15 4v16" /></svg>
          </div>
          <div class="understanding-content">
            <div class="understanding-source"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 3H6v18h12V7zM14 3v5h5M9 12h6m-6 4h6" /></svg> Your lecture, simplified</div>
            <h2>Same transformation.<br />A simpler point of view.</h2>
            <p>Choose an eigenvector basis, and a complicated transformation becomes just a stretch.</p>
            <div class="understanding-equation math" aria-label="A equals P times D times P inverse">
              <span>A</span><span>=</span><span class="factor-back">P</span><span class="factor-stretch">D</span><span class="factor-basis">P<sup>−1</sup></span>
            </div>
            <ol class="understanding-steps">
              <li class="step-basis"><span class="step-symbol math">P<sup>−1</sup></span><div><h3>Change your view</h3><p>Write x in the eigenvector basis.</p></div></li>
              <li class="step-stretch"><span class="step-symbol math">D</span><div><h3>Just stretch</h3><p>Scale along each eigenvector.</p></div></li>
              <li class="step-back"><span class="step-symbol math">P</span><div><h3>Change back</h3><p>Return to the original coordinates.</p></div></li>
            </ol>
            <div class="understanding-takeaway"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 12 4 4L19 6" /></svg><p>Read right to left. Three small steps, one transformation.</p></div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="transformation-controls" role="group" aria-label="Compare the lecture with EdU’s explanation">
        <button type="button" data-view-button="lecture" aria-pressed="true">The lecture</button>
        <button type="button" data-view-button="understood" aria-pressed="false"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m12 3 2.5 6.5L21 12l-6.5 2.5L12 21l-2.5-6.5L3 12l6.5-2.5Z" /></svg> With EdU</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <a class="hero-explore" href="#how-it-works">See how it works <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v16m-5-5 5 5 5-5" /></svg></a>
</transformation-hero>

<script>
  import "./transformation";
</script>
